# Response headers for cbfw.us (Cloudflare Workers static assets).
# Vite copies this file into dist/; Cloudflare reads it and does not serve it.
#
# WHY A CSP. The Supabase session lives in the browser, so one script injected
# into the page is a stolen account. RichText renders posts as React nodes and
# never as HTML, which is the first line; this is the second, so that a future
# slip in the first does not hand the session to another origin.
#
# WHAT IT ALLOWS, AND WHY EACH:
#   script-src  'self': one module bundle plus its lazy chunks, no inline
#               script anywhere. And Cloudflare Web Analytics' beacon, which
#               Cloudflare injects into the page on this zone: the first CSP
#               (2026-11-24) said it did not, and blocked it on production
#               the same day (seen 11-25). Drop both cloudflareinsights hosts
#               if Web Analytics is ever switched off.
#   style-src   'unsafe-inline' for the two static pages (privacy.html and
#               terms.html each carry a <style> block). A style cannot run code.
#   connect-src the Supabase project: REST, auth, storage and the Realtime
#               socket; and cloudflareinsights.com, where the beacon reports. The project's URL is the VITE_SUPABASE_URL repository
#               variable; CHANGE THIS LINE IF THE PROJECT EVER MOVES, or every
#               query is refused.
#   img-src     the same project's storage (post images, signed images), plus
#               data: and blob: for game icons and image uploads in the editor.
#
# A LOCAL `pnpm build` points at 127.0.0.1:54321, which this policy refuses.
# That bundle must never be deployed (CLAUDE.md), so nothing is lost; serve
# dist/ through `vite preview`, which does not read this file, to look at it.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://balpuvkvpiqvclibajje.supabase.co; connect-src 'self' https://balpuvkvpiqvclibajje.supabase.co wss://balpuvkvpiqvclibajje.supabase.co https://cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# Vite puts a content hash in every file name under /assets/, so a file there
# never changes: cache it for a year. index.html keeps Cloudflare's default
# (max-age=0, must-revalidate), which is what makes a release show up at once.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
